{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3118","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3118","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3118\",\"parent_revision\":\"30ae18aaed33f6fec913eee05f6c80144190e448\",\"root_revision\":\"e523920a183c821e0b71caec9760fc85ee19b065787ed4a3b16dd73e5826334f\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nDuring the #3060 incident investigation, a worktree-isolated agent's own git worktree vanished mid-task, unexplained. It was investigated at the time \u2014 no dangling ref was found, and no evidence of a prune operation was found. The cause remains genuinely unknown, not just undocumented.\\n\\nWhen it happens, the agent loses its working directory mid-task and downstream commands fail unpredictably. See related items on Bash cwd reset and the git-blocking guard behavior after a worktree is lost.\\n\\nObserved once during this session; not yet reproduced.\\n\\n**User-provided context**: Full evidence trail recorded at `.tmp/scratch/reports/20260821-task-worker-over-orchestration.md`.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **worktree-isolated agent's git worktree vanished mid-task (cause unknown)** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation - #3060 incident investigation\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-22\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"546077019dfd6bc7240635c1ec35300ed9d6449d2dfc70b2f8a746cfe984f172\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABXPQwlQ\"}"}